        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "6fe16a36-369c-36cd-a747-08e5a5229200",
                "word": "ouvertement",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f6f0f60a-b7f8-3eb2-a679-43da2331ba7f",
                        "entry_id": "6fe16a36-369c-36cd-a747-08e5a5229200",
                        "glosses": [
                            "D’une manière ouverte, manifeste."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c3c6ff21-3f0e-4a41-a294-4f659eb856e3",
                                "sense_id": "f6f0f60a-b7f8-3eb2-a679-43da2331ba7f",
                                "text": "Il est bien pénible de voir renverser toute la morale chrétienne par des égarements si étranges, sans oser y contredire ouvertement,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "895d6189-3a8c-405d-b81b-b24c674beb4e",
                                "sense_id": "f6f0f60a-b7f8-3eb2-a679-43da2331ba7f",
                                "text": "C'est l’ordinaire des orgueilleux d’exercer ouvertement leurs inimitiés,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3f15c46b-538b-41cd-88d1-280662eb1c71",
                                "sense_id": "f6f0f60a-b7f8-3eb2-a679-43da2331ba7f",
                                "text": "Marc-Aurèle ordonna qu’on ne poursuivît point les chrétiens pour cause de religion ; Caracalla, Héliogabale, Alexandre, Philippe, Gallien les protégèrent ouvertement,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2307c552-615e-41cd-8324-aebb8c21161e",
                                "sense_id": "f6f0f60a-b7f8-3eb2-a679-43da2331ba7f",
                                "text": "Il est certaines situations dont bénéficient seuls les gens tarés. Ils fondent leur fortune là où des hommes mieux posés et plus influents n’auraient point osé risquer la leur. Certes, Roudier, Granoux et les autres, par leur position d’hommes riches et respectés, semblaient devoir être mille fois préférés à Pierre comme chefs actifs du parti conservateur. Mais aucun d’eux n’aurait consenti à faire de son salon un centre politique ; leurs convictions n’allaient pas jusqu’à se compromettre ouvertement ; en somme, ce n’étaient que des braillards, des commères de province, qui voulaient bien cancaner chez un voisin contre la République, du moment où le voisin endossait la responsabilité de leurs cancans."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "534cd9ec-6737-4b92-a242-ea6156f71ff5",
                                "sense_id": "f6f0f60a-b7f8-3eb2-a679-43da2331ba7f",
                                "text": "Non contents de traquer les fourrageurs et d'enlever les hommes isolés, les Indiens commençaient à menacer ouvertement la place."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b988a0a5-6cb9-44f7-b724-229df7df782a",
                                "sense_id": "f6f0f60a-b7f8-3eb2-a679-43da2331ba7f",
                                "text": "Brest, exceptionnelle enclave, est, en somme, la seule commune où un esprit anticlérical, se manifeste ouvertement."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "19d3431a-eeca-4991-b4ee-3d646d4dbb5b",
                                "sense_id": "f6f0f60a-b7f8-3eb2-a679-43da2331ba7f",
                                "text": "Entre temps, les rationalistes zélés avaient dû prendra garde aux poursuites d'un cléricalisme obscurantin. Ils furent obligés de ne pas manifester trop ouvertement leurs vues, en raison de la « crainte du sabre »."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b3465f74-7151-4c05-aafe-4db71a07bcea",
                        "source_entry_id": "6fe16a36-369c-36cd-a747-08e5a5229200",
                        "source_sense_id": "f6f0f60a-b7f8-3eb2-a679-43da2331ba7f",
                        "target_lang_word": "openly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "openly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c8453ead-e2b5-3d11-9932-969e50d063d9",
                                        "entry_id": "0ff5e0eb-4807-374b-ae3f-e7449d1a78d3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In an open manner; visibly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01c062ac-f4ae-41bd-b3c5-6b1e6f4b2bd3",
                                                "sense_id": "c8453ead-e2b5-3d11-9932-969e50d063d9",
                                                "text": "Nevertheless, without openly admitting it, he was devoted to Boxer;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf11c3e8-806d-49c5-be06-ca0cac028e71",
                                                "sense_id": "c8453ead-e2b5-3d11-9932-969e50d063d9",
                                                "text": "The openly ridiculous plot has The Pirate Captain (Hugh Grant) scheming to win the Pirate Of The Year competition, even though he’s a terrible pirate, far outclassed by rivals voiced by Jeremy Piven and Salma Hayek."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27d97819-ef94-4156-a2ed-14ea7f0d819d",
                                                "sense_id": "c8453ead-e2b5-3d11-9932-969e50d063d9",
                                                "text": "We must speak our minds openly, debate our disagreements honestly, but always pursue solidarity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4c7f7b9-05ee-416f-a6df-65c3f5beabc7",
                                                "sense_id": "c8453ead-e2b5-3d11-9932-969e50d063d9",
                                                "text": "Particular note, in this period, should be made of the actions of Joseph Denman, commander of the Northern Division of the Squadron, who went on an absolutely ruthless and systematic campaign along the African coast, burning so-called \"slaving factories\" to the ground and openly daring anyone who objected to try and stop him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71597a6a-9739-4ee8-823e-4493312d2460",
                                                "sense_id": "c8453ead-e2b5-3d11-9932-969e50d063d9",
                                                "text": "When a column of smoke appeared on Thursday over the Sitong Bridge overpass in the Haidian district of Beijing, it drew attention to a protester who had hung banners openly bashing China’s top leader by name and criticizing the country’s “zero Covid” policy, including one calling for “freedom and not lockdowns.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6c56cea8-6946-49b8-b2f9-aba9df7375f1",
                        "source_entry_id": "6fe16a36-369c-36cd-a747-08e5a5229200",
                        "source_sense_id": "f6f0f60a-b7f8-3eb2-a679-43da2331ba7f",
                        "target_lang_word": "frankly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "frankly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c91877a8-dfc8-3eed-b73e-9f133ae51c5e",
                                        "entry_id": "de1d0147-e884-32fb-aeae-8a560f77fc4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a frank or candid manner, especially in a way that may seem too open, excessively honest, or slightly blunt."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d917adc-5ad2-45f2-b041-7720788013be",
                                                "sense_id": "c91877a8-dfc8-3eed-b73e-9f133ae51c5e",
                                                "text": "to speak frankly"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3691d12-7429-4a15-86b9-ce7ab309d35b",
                                                "sense_id": "c91877a8-dfc8-3eed-b73e-9f133ae51c5e",
                                                "text": "He spoke frankly about the economy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d26d4812-01f7-4253-a57d-b9497fb60ccd",
                                                "sense_id": "c91877a8-dfc8-3eed-b73e-9f133ae51c5e",
                                                "text": "She was frankly disappointed. For some reason she had expected to discover a burglar of one or another accepted type—either a dashing cracksman in full-blown evening dress, lithe, polished, pantherish, or a common yegg, a red-eyed, unshaven, burly brute in the rags and tatters of a tramp."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b40b90d0-d586-436d-b33a-e423048a13e4",
                                                "sense_id": "c91877a8-dfc8-3eed-b73e-9f133ae51c5e",
                                                "text": "Musk’s Israel tour was transparently transactional and frankly insulting. The antisemitic sentiment Musk endorsed had nothing to do with Israel; “replacement theory” is generally an unsupported allegation that Jews and other immigrants in the US and Europe are destroying Western civilization."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7181f7f2-cb33-31b1-8809-f554251adbb1",
                                        "entry_id": "de1d0147-e884-32fb-aeae-8a560f77fc4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In truth, to tell the truth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f0052798-643d-4610-932f-23cd481d6a53",
                                                "sense_id": "7181f7f2-cb33-31b1-8809-f554251adbb1",
                                                "text": "Most of what they said was, frankly, a pack of lies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ff91139-86c5-4c09-886c-f5c251dcce1c",
                                                "sense_id": "7181f7f2-cb33-31b1-8809-f554251adbb1",
                                                "text": "Frankly, my dear, I don't give a damn."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6736cd47-898e-3ebb-a9da-65d9c81555b1",
                                        "entry_id": "de1d0147-e884-32fb-aeae-8a560f77fc4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To a degree large enough as to be plainly evident."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c4c9c42-8cce-4b1a-91cd-b9301345a126",
                                                "sense_id": "6736cd47-898e-3ebb-a9da-65d9c81555b1",
                                                "text": "frankly septic"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "496ecd1d-1842-4847-9119-f966b07f1e51",
                                                "sense_id": "6736cd47-898e-3ebb-a9da-65d9c81555b1",
                                                "text": "frankly psychotic"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
